#import "release.typ": release, plain-words, signing
#show: release.with(
  title: "Mutual Confidentiality Agreement",
  intro: [*Thank you for being part of the crew.* This is the agreement between you and Sun Brewed Homestead Inc. ("the Homestead") as a volunteer, crew member or board member. Each of us will see private information the other, or people who trust us, care about, and we both promise to protect it. The Homestead is bound by this agreement from the moment it sends it to you for signature. Below, "I" means you.],
)

#plain-words[
- We both keep private what we learn about each other and about the people we serve: donors, members, volunteers, adopters and especially children.
- We use it only for Homestead work, and share it only with people who need it.
- You can always report wrongdoing, harassment or anything unlawful to the authorities or a lawyer. Nothing here stops you.
]

*1. The Homestead's confidential information.* The personal details of donors, members, volunteers, workshop participants and adopters (names, contact details, addresses, donation amounts and histories); anything about minors; the Homestead's non-public finances, budgets, grant applications and fundraising plans; gate, lock and alarm codes, passwords and account access; internal discussions in private channels (for example the Leadership and Farm ops areas of our Discord); and anything marked or reasonably understood to be confidential.

*2. My confidential information.* My contact details and address, my emergency contact, any health condition, allergy or accommodation I tell the Homestead about, background-check and training records, incident reports about me, and anything else I share in confidence.

*3. What we each agree to.* Each of us will use the other's confidential information only for Homestead work, share it only with people who need it for that work (for example, a lead on shift who needs to know about an allergy, or emergency responders), and protect it with at least reasonable care. I will not copy donor or member lists or take them with me, will keep passwords and codes private, and will report any suspected leak to a Steward promptly. The Homestead will never sell or rent my information, will keep it in access-controlled systems, will tell me promptly if a leak affects it, and will delete it when I ask once it no longer needs it, except records the law or its insurance requires it to keep.

*4. What this does not cover.* Information that is already public through no fault of the person receiving it, that they knew before, or that they are required by law or court order to disclose (after telling the other, where the law allows) is not covered. *Nothing in this agreement prevents me from discussing or disclosing information about unlawful acts, such as harassment or discrimination or any other conduct that I have reason to believe is unlawful,* or from reporting possible wrongdoing to a government agency, law enforcement or an attorney, discussing my own volunteer experience, or making any disclosure the law protects or requires.

*5. Defend Trade Secrets Act notice.* Under 18 U.S.C. § 1833(b), an individual is not liable under trade secret law for disclosing a trade secret in confidence to a government official or an attorney solely to report or investigate a suspected violation of law, or in a sealed court filing.

*6. When I leave.* When my role ends, I will return or delete Homestead materials and leave any Homestead accounts and groups I was given access to. Both of our obligations continue after I leave.

#signing[*7. General.* Because a leak of someone's private information can't be undone with money, either of us may ask a court to stop a breach, in addition to any other remedy. This agreement is not a contract of employment and does not create any right to a role or payment. It is governed by California law. If any part is held unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. I agree to sign electronically, and my electronic signature binds me as if written by hand. *I have read this agreement and had the chance to ask questions about it, and I sign it voluntarily.*]
